up factor problem asks whether the von Neumann algebras of free groups of different ranks are isomorphic. The formalization proves that interpolated free group factors with any parameters $r,s>1$, including the infinite parameter, are normally trace-preservingly isomorphic. The paper's fundamental-group conclusion is a further consequence rather than a separate selected statement here.","title":"Isomorphism of the free group factors","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/docs/287.md"}},"provenance":{"kind":"computed-navigation","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","rule":"Projection of the pinned ledger; no new mathematical assessment."},"reader_comparison":{"headline_coverage":"disagree","method":"Compare reported scope categories; notes remain attributed and are not adjudicated.","points":[{"definitions_to_check":null,"gap":"The fundamental-group clause is not stated; it is a (short, unformalized) consequence of the stated isomorphisms.","note":null,"reading":"reading:5937ba79c80864ee10f2fb0a","source_term":"NARROWER — DECLARED","state":"narrower"},{"definitions_to_check":"Hand-built II_1 factor models: `groupVonNeumann G := centralizer (centralizer (leftTranslations G))` (double commutant of left translations), `canonicalTrace`, `ultraweakOperatorTopology := ⨅ ξ η, induced (T ↦ Σ' k ⟨η k, T (ξ k)⟩)`, corners `Corner p hp` and `selectedProjection a := Classical.epsilon (stabilizedProjectionTrace p = ofReal a)` (junk default projection 0 if none existed, which does not happen in L(F_2)⊗B(ℓ²)); standard but not Mathlib's `VonNeumannAlgebra`-with-trace.","gap":null,"note":"`allInterpolatedIsomorphic (r s : ℝ≥0∞) (hr : 1 < r) (hs : 1 < s) : Nonempty (NormalTracialEquiv (interpolatedTrace r) (interpolatedTrace s) (interpolatedTopology r) (interpolatedTopology s))`: every pair of interpolated free group factors L(F_r), L(F_s) with r,s ∈ (1,∞] (integer ranks via `