ropy-dimensions","section":7,"section_title":"Free entropy dimensions and von Neumann generators","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","file":"preprints/An-isomorphism-of-the-free-group-factors-September-23-2026/build/sections/entropy-dimensions.tex","line":21,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"368cd65b850ed94085ef3f8590dd0659aa41573a169f3adf65b63a077232cd9f","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/An-isomorphism-of-the-free-group-factors-September-23-2026/build/sections/entropy-dimensions.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:23ca61d5d9dab5fafee8d1c99b830d67e36fc6313558ed254a056e75cd15cf2a","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/An-isomorphism-of-the-free-group-factors-September-23-2026/build/sections/entropy-dimensions.tex#L21"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:entropy-dimensions}\nLet $M=L(\\F_2)$ with its canonical trace. For every integer $n\\geq2$\nthere are a self-adjoint $n$-tuple $X^{(n)}$ and a self-adjoint\n$2n$-tuple $Y^{(n)}$ such that\n\\[\n W^*(X^{(n)})=W^*(Y^{(n)})=M\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n \\delta(X^{(n)})=\\delta_0(X^{(n)})=n,\n \\qquad\n \\delta^*(Y^{(n)})=\\delta^\\star(Y^{(n)})=n.\n\\]\nConsequently, none of $\\delta,\\delta_0,\\delta^*,\\delta^\\star$ is\ninvariant under changing a finite self-adjoint $W^*$-generating tuple\nof a tracial von Neumann algebra. Each takes unbounded values on such\ngenerating tuples of the single factor $L(\\F_2)$."}],"unavailable_check_reports":[]}
